@startuml boomletwo_checkpoint_recovery
title Self-contained DIGGING checkpoint and Boomletwo activation
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 75
participant "Original Boomlet" as B
participant Niso as N
participant WT as W
participant "Other peers" as P
participant "Designated offline Boomletwo" as T
participant "Enrolled ST" as S
participant "Setup-bound SAR" as R
actor "User" as U

note over B,T
  Only peers with a designated setup backup create these checkpoints.
  Setup has authorized exactly this target.
  Neither ST nor Boomletwo records each ordinary transition.
  The checkpoint format below is a candidate extension.
end note

group Normal DIGGING
  B -> B: Validate progress; preserve exact SAR duty,\nconsent counter, rotation records, replies and consumed budgets
  B -> B: Create target-encrypted checkpoint and exact placeholder
  B -> B: Bind checkpoint digest in existing signed ping
  B -> N: Signed ping bundle with detached encrypted checkpoint
  N -> W: Ordinary authenticated submission with recovery bundle
  W -> P: Retain checkpoint evidence under the candidate distribution policy
  W -> W: Collect five pings and exact recipient SAR acknowledgments
  W -> B: Candidate shared five-ping pong and own SAR acknowledgment
  B -> B: Match own returned ping; verify the other four\nKeep ordinary counter and SAR guards
end

... Original Boomlet is lost; no further source interaction ...
destroy B

group Inspect a recovery checkpoint
  U -> T: Start recovery using designated setup backup
  N -> T: Retained ping bundle and required public evidence
  P -> T: Existing WT activation record and available decision evidence
  T -> T: Verify source signature and exact encrypted checkpoint\nBind setup, target, withdrawal, sequence and placeholder
  T -> T: Identify WT at the checkpoint using retained head\nDo not treat peer claims as latest-state authority
  note over N,T
    A valid old ping can omit later duress, consent transitions or WT votes.
  end note
end

group Independent activation
  T -> T: Bind saved activation nonce and stored key pair\nSign setup-bound replacement using imported Boomlet identity key
  T -> S: Authenticated activation query and signed replacement proposal
  S -> U: Review setup and replacement; show stored consent counter\nPresent fresh country query
  U -> S: Country response
  S -> T: Authenticated response bound to saved query
  T -> T: Consume response durably\nunder_duress := saved_under_duress OR mismatch
  T -> R: Saved encrypted activation placeholder through Niso\nBind setup, key pair and nonce; use imported SAR channel
  R -> R: Apply identical safe and duress processing and acknowledgment delay
  R -> T: Acknowledgment of exact saved placeholder through Niso
  T -> T: Verify acknowledgment; sign inner signed message with own key\nCommit ACTIVE and exact replacement certificate before output
  T -> N: Doubly signed key replacement certificate
  N -> P: Saved replacement certificate
  N -> W: Saved replacement certificate
  N -> S: Saved replacement certificate
  N -> R: Saved replacement certificate
  note over P,R
    Each recipient verifies both signatures, setup and key fields.
    Atomically store certificate and accepted identity before acknowledgment.
    Accept future actions for that peer only under Boomletwo's key.
    Exact retries recover the saved result; retain historical evidence.
  end note
end

alt Complete withdrawal state and required evidence have been recovered
  T -> T: Bind checkpoint and attempt irreversibly\nGenerate and persist one independent draw R
  T -> T: For unreached state use max(original mystery, R)\nor setup upper bound plus R
  T -> T: Restore only authenticated progress and exact duties\nContinue ordinary gates under replacement identity
else Withdrawal state or later security history is unresolved
  T -> T: Retain accepted identity and recovered evidence\nWait before signing, WT voting or new counter progress
end

note over P,T
  Setup ID, descriptor and peer ordering stay fixed across replacement.
  Historical pongs and ping counts cannot earn new counter increments.
  Earlier rescue duties require recovery independently of the new duress check.
end note
@enduml
